From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:34:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add a Facebook Messenger protocol (prpl-gometa) to the plugin

Register a second prpl, prpl-gometa ("Facebook (E2EE)"), from the same
shared object. It talks to Messenger through messagix
(go.mau.fi/mautrix-meta/pkg/messagix) and handles end-to-end encrypted
threads through whatsmeow's Facebook (armadillo) client. It has to live
in this plugin rather than in one of its own: whatsmeow and messagix are
both Go, and two Go c-archives cannot share one process, so both
protocols run on this plugin's Go runtime. All of its identifiers are
prefixed gometa to stay clear of the WhatsApp code.

- gometa.go: login with e-mail, password and an interactive second
  factor (the session is cached in the account), contact and thread
  sync, incoming messages, plaintext sends, presence
- gometa_e2ee.go: E2EE threads - registration, sending, reactions and
  receipts; a plaintext send that Facebook does not confirm is retried
  over E2EE and the thread remembered as encrypted
- gometa_media.go, gometa_video.go: pictures, voice notes, video and
  documents, plaintext and E2EE
- gometabridge.[ch], glue/gometa_init.c: the C side and the prpl
  registration
- incoming E2EE media is downloaded through the Facebook client
  (fbDownloadable) and shown like WhatsApp media; download_attachment()
  now recovers from a panic, which would otherwise abort the whole
  process from inside a cgo call
- the account-removed and send-reaction handlers of the webOS
  integration also serve prpl-gometa accounts, and deleting one removes
  its gometa-e2ee-<user>.db

go.mod pins mautrix-meta v0.2607.0 and mirrors the beeper/req replace
that its messagix package needs. On top of 1.27.0's whatsmeow, mautrix
moves to v0.32.0 (v0.29.0 does not build against go.mau.fi/util v0.11.0)
and the beeper/req replace moves to v3.0.0-20260925135712-b49593750e56
(the older one does not build against quic-go v0.61.0). mautrix-meta
v0.2608.0 and later rename the messagix events and split
types.MessengerLite, and are not used yet.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS addition, not part of purple-gowhatsapp]
